From 9228d0bcfefcc2dfdd0e92b269591a0cb40ecc82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:45:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0045-vela-unity-vk-interface: the 0044 code patch lands too
 late when OptiScaler is loaded after the plugin device init (device job R8D),
 so Unity is asked through its own public interface instead. IUnityInterfaces*
 is read from the global NVUnityPlugin.dll keeps it in: the export
 UnityPluginLoad, its E9 jump thunks, the first RIP-relative 64-bit store in
 the first 0x80 bytes (decoded, no fixed RVA; this build: RVA 154268); every
 pointer is checked (readable, function pointers inside UnityPlayer.dll)
 before a call. IUnityGraphicsVulkan = GetInterfaceSplit(V1 GUID
 95355348d4ef4e11-9789313dfcffcc87); V1 and V2 share the slots used (2
 ConfigureEvent, 4 CommandRecordingState, 9 EnsureOutsideRenderPass).
 VELA_UNITY_VK_OUTSIDE is now bit flags, unset = 7: 1 = the 0044 patch; 2 =
 ConfigureEvent(NVUP_GetBaseEventId()+1 and +2, {EnsureOutside, DontCare, 9})
 at NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_Init and once more before the first recording call; 4 =
 before CreateFeature and Evaluate record: CommandRecordingState, inside a
 render pass -> EnsureOutsideRenderPass, state again, and recording goes into
 the command buffer Unity then names. 0043 interplay: in auto mode the answer
 of Unity wins (outside -> not deferred, still inside -> deferred, call failed
 or no interface -> the rules as before). Log prefix Vela Unity VK: (interface
 found, ConfigureEvent events, first CreateFeature / Evaluate state, counters
 every 600 Evaluate calls, one line per failure). VelaVkDefer::DropHandle also
 waits up to 200 ms each for jobs of the handle already on the GPU before the
 feature is destroyed (VUID-vkDestroyImage-image-01000 in run R8C). Host test:
 the decode on the real plugin gives function RVA 35DD0 and global RVA 154268

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
